## Change review - 2026-10-28

**Graph projections expose partial coverage and invalidate changed generations before returning evidence.** Reviewed commit `c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8` (commit date `2026-10-26T19:06:20+05:30`). Compared with `2a00e7b38fc4ae4e38af4134586be0bbe9612706`; the complete Git comparison contains 733 changed paths.

The graph retrieval index separates canonical records from bounded projections and hashed postings, records truncation as indexIncomplete/incompleteRecords, and uses build/revision-bound cursors. Pending writes and recovery journals prevent readers from accepting an unfinished view; journal replay uses absolute edits and fixtures cover lost acknowledgements, generation reset, stale cursors, corruption and request-isolated cancellation. Readers cap point reads, serialized decoded bytes and active concurrency, cache index records only, and recheck generation/revision at finish. GraphQuery refreshes current source observations before emitting bounded titles and invokes an optional authorization callback; secure ownership therefore depends on the caller supplying it. Bytes are accounted after the underlying get returns, not before engine allocation; documentation explicitly excludes strict end-to-end deadlines and identifies bulk legacy migration and a still-enumerating MCP stats resource. The embedding wrapper rejects wrong dimensions but does not check finite values or returned batch cardinality.

Evidence: [src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts:79-170](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts#L79-L170) · [src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts:238-291](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts#L238-L291) · [src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts:397-495](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/src/state/graph-retrieval-index.ts#L397-L495) · [src/functions/graph-retrieval.ts:73-122](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/src/functions/graph-retrieval.ts#L73-L122) · [test/graph-retrieval-index.test.ts:88-207](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/test/graph-retrieval-index.test.ts#L88-L207) · [src/providers/embedding/index.ts:52-80](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/src/providers/embedding/index.ts#L52-L80) · [docs/reliability/graph-search-budget.md:1-13](https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory/blob/c5b8ebfb32eb6a08fe301d3bb75840f3597b66c8/docs/reliability/graph-search-budget.md#L1-L13).

**Harness consequence:** Use bounded derived projections as disposable retrieval accelerators, retain canonical source evidence, mark incomplete coverage and discard stale generation results. Make source authorization mandatory at Teamagent's adapter boundary. Add transport allocation/admission limits beyond post-read accounting, and validate embedding cardinality, finite values, model/revision and dimensions together. Keep explicit migration and bulk maintenance separate from ordinary searches.

**Scope and limits:** Scoped static review of graph index budgets/recovery, selected evidence-finalization and embedding guards in the 733-path comparison. The complete changed repository, underlying KV engine, all authorization call sites and migration implementation were not audited. Tests were read, not run; no model, storage-load or recovery experiment was performed.

